{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Confirmed RCA: tests/_stall_remote.py sends one fixed rate//10 chunk per loop, so delayed 0.1-second wake-ups permanently reduce actual throughput below the rate promised by the fixture. With forced 0.55-second wake-ups, real Git reported the 1000 B/s low-speed abort in 2/2 trials while every send gap stayed below 0.56 seconds; cumulative elapsed-time pacing held about 4000 B/s and returned only the expected malformed-protocol failure in 2/2. The defect is test-only: production floor/window values remain correct and unchanged."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786447075918577001,"uuid":"3bde9d8b-2f6c-45b9-a996-3e712b817da4"}